# Managed by Ansible (roles/k8s-apps). Edits on the host will be overwritten.
#
# No longer a split horizon, despite the filename. It was written when public
# DNS answered these names with the master's Tailscale address, unreachable
# outside the tailnet, so LAN clients needed the ingress VIP from here instead.
# Since 2026-08-23 external-dns publishes that same VIP (ingress_status_address
# now resolves to ingress_lan_address), so both sides return one address and
# this file agrees with the public record rather than overriding it.
#
# Kept because it is still load-bearing in one direction: these names keep
# resolving on the LAN when Cloudflare, external-dns or the uplink is down, and
# a query answered locally never leaves the house. Delete it only if you are
# content for internal name resolution to depend on an external record.
#
# Leaf hostnames are listed individually on purpose: dnsmasq's address=/domain/
# also matches the apex, and krugten.org itself is a GitHub Pages site that must
# keep resolving to its public address.
{% for host in ingress_objects.resources
     | map(attribute='spec.rules')
     | flatten
     | map(attribute='host')
     | select('defined') | unique | sort %}
address=/{{ host }}/{{ ingress_lan_address }}
{% endfor %}
